# `circuit::Circuit::unknowns`

[Back to `circuit::Circuit`](../CircuitModel.md)

The number of unknowns of the nodal equations.

## Signature

```cpp
std::int64_t circuit::Circuit::unknowns() const noexcept;
```

## What It Does

Returns the size of the linear system solved at each operating point: the non-ground node voltages, plus one current for every voltage source, inductor, voltage-controlled voltage source and op amp. Use it to size anything that accompanies a solution. It does not depend on batch axes.

## Returns

The number of unknowns.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

Two node voltages and the source current make three unknowns.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace ckt = pluss::subsp::eng::circuit;
using namespace pluss::tils;

static pluss::Series vec(std::vector<double> v) { return pluss::series::make(v); }

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  ckt::Net net;
  net.nodes = 3;
  net.voltage_sources = {{1}, {0}, vec({10.0})};
  net.resistors = {{1, 2}, {2, 0}, vec({1000.0, 3000.0})};
  const ckt::Circuit obj = ckt::make(net);
  out.writeln("unknowns =", obj.unknowns(), " nodes", obj.nodes());
}
```

### Example 2

A circuit using every linear element: resistor, capacitor, inductor, both sources, both controlled sources and an op amp.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace ckt = pluss::subsp::eng::circuit;
using namespace pluss::tils;

static pluss::Series vec(std::vector<double> v) { return pluss::series::make(v); }

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  ckt::Net net;
  net.nodes = 6;
  net.resistors = {{1}, {2}, vec({1000.0})};
  net.capacitors = {{2}, {0}, vec({1e-6})};
  net.inductors = {{2}, {3}, vec({1e-3})};
  net.current_sources = {{0}, {3}, vec({0.001})};
  net.voltage_sources = {{1}, {0}, vec({5.0})};
  net.vccs = {{4}, {0}, {1}, {0}, vec({0.002})};
  net.vcvs = {{5}, {0}, {1}, {0}, vec({2.0})};
  net.amps = {{4}, {0}, {0}, {3}};
  const ckt::Circuit obj = ckt::make(net);
  out.writeln("unknowns =", obj.unknowns(), " nodes", obj.nodes());
}
```

### Example 3

Batching does not change the size of one circuit's system.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace ckt = pluss::subsp::eng::circuit;
using namespace pluss::tils;

static pluss::Series vec(std::vector<double> v) { return pluss::series::make(v); }

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  ckt::Net net;
  net.nodes = 3;
  net.voltage_sources = {{1}, {0}, vec({10.0})};
  net.resistors = {{1, 2}, {2, 0}, vec({1000, 1000, 1000, 2000, 1000, 4000}).reshape({3, 2})};
  const ckt::Circuit obj = ckt::make(net);
  out.writeln("unknowns =", obj.unknowns(), " nodes", obj.nodes());
}
```

